# Rot-Curse Rakshasa: "Trample. Decayed (This creature can't block. When it attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat.)"
# Decayed (CR 702.147a) is "this creature can't block" and "when this creature attacks, sacrifice it at end of combat".
# On turn 3 the 5/5 attacks and Bot2's Embereth Shieldbreaker (2/1) blocks: trample assigns 1 to the blocker and 4 to Bot2
# (CR 702.19b). Its attack trigger set up "sacrifice it at end of combat", at the beginning of the end of combat step
# (CR 511.2), so after the damage it goes to the graveyard; the 2 damage the Shieldbreaker dealt would not have killed it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Rot-Curse Rakshasa
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rot-Curse Rakshasa.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Embereth Shieldbreaker.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rot-Curse Rakshasa > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Embereth Shieldbreaker > Rot-Curse Rakshasa)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Rot-Curse Rakshasa > Embereth Shieldbreaker: 1; Rot-Curse Rakshasa > Bot2: 4)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 16
Bot2.Graveyard = Embereth Shieldbreaker
Bot1.Graveyard = Rot-Curse Rakshasa
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet
